PART 9: UNDERSTANDING CLEANUP
================================================================================

Timer Effect:

useEffect(() => {

  const timerId =
    setInterval(
      callback,
      intervalMs
    )


  return () => {

    clearInterval(
      timerId
    )

  }

}, [
  intervalMs
])


================================================================================
WHEN DOES CLEANUP RUN?
================================================================================

Cleanup runs:

• Before the Effect is set up again because dependencies changed

• When the component leaves the UI

• During additional development Effect checks where applicable


================================================================================
WITHOUT CLEANUP
================================================================================

Timer 1:

1000ms


User changes:

2000ms


Timer 2 starts.


But Timer 1 remains active.


Result:

Timer 1
+
Timer 2
+
Potential future timers


This creates incorrect timer behavior.


================================================================================
WITH CLEANUP
================================================================================

Old Timer
    ↓
clearInterval()
    ↓
Stopped
    ↓
New Timer
    ↓
Only Current Timer Active


================================================================================
CLEANUP COMPARISON
================================================================================

+--------------------------+---------------------------+
| WITHOUT CLEANUP          | WITH CLEANUP              |
+--------------------------+---------------------------+
| Old timer keeps running  | Old timer stops           |
| Multiple timers possible | One current timer         |
| Incorrect count speed    | Predictable behavior      |
| Resources wasted         | Proper resource cleanup   |
+--------------------------+---------------------------+


