PART 18: COMMON MISTAKES
================================================================================

MISTAKE 1:
ASSUMING [] MEANS GUARANTEED EXACTLY ONCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Better mental model:

[] =
No changing reactive dependencies


Development Strict Mode may perform additional setup/cleanup cycles.


================================================================================
MISTAKE 2:
OMITTING A DEPENDENCY THAT EFFECT USES
================================================================================

Effect:

fetchUser(
  userId
)


Dependency:

[]


Problem:

Effect uses userId but doesn't react when it changes.


================================================================================
MISTAKE 3:
ADDING count TO TIMER DEPENDENCIES UNNECESSARILY
================================================================================

If timer uses:

setCount(
  previous =>
    previous + 1
)


then:

count


doesn't need to be read by the Effect.


================================================================================
MISTAKE 4:
FORGETTING TIMER CLEANUP
================================================================================

Without:

clearInterval()


old timers can remain active.


================================================================================
MISTAKE 5:
THINKING clearTimeout CANCELS AN ACTIVE FETCH
================================================================================

clearTimeout():

Cancels the timer before callback starts.


AbortController:

Cancels the fetch after it has started.


================================================================================
MISTAKE 6:
SEARCHING ON EVERY KEYSTROKE WHEN NOT DESIRED
================================================================================

Dependency:

[searchTerm]


does NOT automatically debounce.


Add:

setTimeout()


with cleanup.


================================================================================
MISTAKE 7:
OBJECT CREATED DURING RENDER AS DEPENDENCY
================================================================================

const filters = {
  category
}


Dependency:

[filters]


This may retrigger unnecessarily because the object reference is recreated.


